 "pulse": "THE PULSE — ATTENTION, MEASURED\nSOURCE: WIKIMEDIA · TOTAL LIVE · COMPARISONS CAPTURED 2026-11-09\nENCYCLOPEDIA READS · ALL TWELVE SIGNS\n14.1K / day\nTRAILING 30 DAYS · EN.WIKIPEDIA\nVS DOGECOIN\n45×\n314 / DAY · SINGLE ARTICLE\nVS ETHEREUM\n20×\n705 / DAY · SINGLE ARTICLE\nVS SOLANA\n51×\n278 / DAY · SINGLE ARTICLE\nVS SHIBA INU\n201×\n70 / DAY · SINGLE ARTICLE\nONE SIGN AT A TIME\nWIKIMEDIA · SINGLE ARTICLES, SAME WINDOW\n\nOne on one: the median sign article reads at 1.4× the Ethereum article, the most read of the four token articles compared here.\n\nAries\n1.1K\nTaurus\n849\nGemini\n2.0K\nCancer\n612\nLeo\n615\nVirgo\n859\nLibra\n1.1K\nScorpio\n1.7K\nSagittarius\n2.1K\nCapricorn\n1.2K\nAquarius\n976\nPisces\n896\n\nReads per day, one disambiguated article per sign. The line marks the Ethereum article in the same window (705 / day). Token articles compared: Dogecoin 314 · Ethereum 705 · Solana 278 · Shiba Inu 70. Bitcoin is not among them: its article had 3,238 reads a day from 10 Oct to 8 Nov 2026, more than any single sign article in those 30 days.\n\nSEARCHING THE SKY\nSOURCE: GOOGLE TRENDS · CAPTURED 2026-11-09 · 12MO RELATIVE\n“horoscope”\n64\n“dogecoin”\n7\n“solana”\n36\n“ethereum”\n44\nOPEN THE LIVE COMPARISON\n↗\nSEARCHING, SIGN BY SIGN\nGOOGLE TRENDS · CAPTURED 2026-11-09 · “DOGECOIN” = 1\n“aries horoscope”\n0.4×\n“taurus horoscope”\n0.4×\n“gemini horoscope”\n0.4×\n“cancer horoscope”\n0.5×\n“leo horoscope”\n0.4×\n“virgo horoscope”\n0.4×\n“libra horoscope”\n0.4×\n“scorpio horoscope”\n0.4×\n“sagittarius horoscope”\n0.3×\n“capricorn horoscope”\n0.3×\n“aquarius horoscope”\n0.3×\n“pisces horoscope”\n0.4×\n\nBare sign terms are ambiguous in English (cancer the disease, gemini the model), so each bar measures the explicit query, an undercount by design. The reference line is the anchor token's search interest over the same twelve months, set to 1.\n\nACROSS THE FEEDS · EDITORIAL ESTIMATES\nESTIMATES · 2026-06\n\nPlatform figures are editorial estimates from public cumulative hashtag and search-volume data — directional, not measured. Encyclopedia figures are measured; search figures are Google Trends relative interest.\n\nX EST.\n≈250K\nASTROLOGY POSTS / DAY\nINSTAGRAM EST.\n≈80K\nSIGN-TAGGED POSTS / DAY\nTIKTOK EST.\n≈100M\nZODIAC-TAG VIEWS / DAY\nGOOGLE EST.\n10M+\n“HOROSCOPE” SEARCHES / MO",
